I step out of the fitting room.
There is a large mirror there.
Near the mirror, there is a red scarf.
It looks very beautiful.
I go near the scarf.
I touch the fabric.
The cotton fabric is very soft.
I check the price.
The price is very low.
This red scarf is cheap.
I put the scarf around my neck.
I look in the large mirror.
This red colour looks good.
I like this scarf a lot.
I call the salesman.
"Dada, I want this scarf," I say.
"Okay, madam," he says.
I put the scarf with my new clothes.
